# WebLogic15c-Installation



                          WebLogic 15.1.1.0.0 Installation
=====================================================================
1.	Copy Binaries on server

 

2.	Verify mountpoint for 15c
a.	/Middleware15c
b.	/Weblogic15c
 

3.	Extract Binaries

Go to cd /Middleware15/Binaries

mv jdk-21.0.10 /Middleware/JAVA

Then execute below command for JDk installation. 
unzip jdk21.zip at Middleware15c  (JDK installation)
mv jdk-21.0.10 to JAVA
unzip webLogic14.1.2.zip

Set JAVA home in .bash_profile. Copy below line in .bash_profile in /home/webadmin

export PATH
export JAVA_HOME=/Middleware15c/JAVA
export PATH=$JAVA_HOME/bin:$PATH

 

4.	Create a oraInst.loc file
[appadmin@SAMUATAPP1 ~]$ cat /Middleware15c/Binaries/oraInst.loc
We need to modify below parameters only. 
inst_group= webadmin
inventory_loc=/Middleware15c/Oracle/oraInventory

5.	Create response file 
[appadmin@SAMUATAPP1 ~]$ cat /Middleware15c/Binaries/wls.rsp
[ENGINE]
Response File Version=1.0.0.0.0
[ENGINE]
ORACLE_HOME=/Middleware15c/Oracle/Oracle_Home
INSTALL_TYPE=WebLogic Server
DECLINE_SECURITY_UPDATES=true
SECURITY_UPDATES_VIA_MYORACLESUPPORT=false
DECLINE_AUTO_UPDATES=true

6.	Install Weblogic 15c, for installation run the following command : 
/Middleware15c/JAVA/bin/java -jar /Middleware15c/Binaries/fmw_15.1.1.0.0_wls.jar -silent -responseFile /Middleware15c/Binaries/wls.rsp -invPtrLoc /Middleware15c/Binaries/oraInst.loc

 
7.	Verify installation
a.	Go to setWLSEnv.sh location
cd /Middleware15c/Oracle/Oracle_Home/wlserver/server/bin/
b.	Execute setWLSEnv.sh
. ./setWLSEnv.sh
c.	Verify the version
/Middleware15c/JAVA/bin/java weblogic.version
 

8.	Create domain 
a.	Create a /Middleware15c/Binaries/domain.py file 

[appadmin@SAMUATAPP1 Binaries]$ cat /Middleware15c/Binaries/domain.py

**************************************** Script start ****************

readTemplate('/Middleware15c/Oracle/Oracle_Home/wlserver/common/templates/wls/wls.jar')
setOption('JavaHome', '/Middleware15c/JAVA')
setOption('ServerStartMode', 'prod')
cd('/Servers/AdminServer')
set('ListenAddress', '10.191.157.175')'ListenAddress', '10.191.157.14')
set('ListenPort', 9001))
cd('/Security/base_domain/User/weblogic')
cmo.setPassword('weblogic123')
writeDomain('/Weblogic15c/user_projects/domains/unipaydomain')
closeTemplate()
exit())

**************************************** Script end ****************
Below will change as per application need 
set('ListenAddress', '10.191.157.175')'ListenAddress', '10.191.157.14')
set('ListenPort', 7004)'ListenPort', 7004)
b.	Execute a domain creation script
/Middleware15c/Oracle/Oracle_Home/oracle_common/common/bin/wlst.sh /Middleware15c/Binaries/domain.py

9.	Start the weblogic server
cd /Weblogic15c/user_projects/domains/unipaydomain/bin
./startWebLogic.sh
10.	 
a.	Create a boot.properties 
cd /Weblogic15c/user_projects/domains/unipaydomain/servers/AdminServer

mkdir security


vi boot.properties 

Add below mentioned lines

username=weblogic
password=weblogic123

b.	cd /Weblogic15c/user_projects/domains/unipaydomain/bin/
c.	nohup ./startWebLogic.sh &
d.	verify the telnet connectivity and logs of admin server 

